# Testing Requirements

- Clarify ambiguity first when requirements are unclear.
- After every task, list edge cases and suggest tests.
- Treat every bug fix as test first: reproduce with a failing test, then fix until it passes.
- After operator correction, document what went wrong and how to prevent it next time.
- `tests/` should mirror `src/`, with shared fixtures in `tests/conftest.py`.
- Cover contract shape, boundary inputs, DB round-trips, idempotency, API failures, and cost accuracy.
- Use mocks for external APIs; do not rely on real network calls in tests.

Run tests with `pytest tests/ -v`.
